# Lazy Stoner Donator Product Data

- Keep `wishlist-products.json`, `js/wishlistProductsData.js`, and the JSON-LD `numberOfItems` in `index.html` synchronized after every product add, removal, replacement, reorder, or tier change.
- Do not invent product facts. Product title, ASIN, marketplace URL, image, availability, and price evidence must come from a product page, user-provided source, manufacturer source, or documented report.
- Amazon.de product URLs should use the canonical PartnerNet format `/dp/ASIN/ref=nosim?tag=cann4chris-21` when the product is actually on Amazon.de.
- Do not add a German PartnerNet tag to Amazon.com or other marketplace URLs. Preserve marketplace-specific URLs exactly when the user supplied or verified them.
- Product cards must not display prices in the visible UI. Price fields may remain in JSON and JSON-LD only for structured data or featured-tier logic.
- If a price is synthetic or only used for layout, set explicit provenance such as `priceSource: "layout_override_user_requested"` and `priceStatus: "layout_override_not_product_price"`.
- Replacements must keep a `replaces` object with old ASIN/title and reason. Prefer current, reputable, orderable alternatives with feature parity over cheap or loosely related products.
- Treat `available`, `unavailable`, and `uncertain` as distinct states. Do not replace an `uncertain` product unless a better verified alternative exists and the trade-off is documented.
- Use high-resolution product images when available and preserve a fallback image path if the primary source is external or non-Amazon.
- After product edits, check removed ASINs/titles, product count, fallback JS data, JSON-LD item count, and JavaScript syntax.
